#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:119
msgid "File Naming"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:122
msgid "Default File Naming"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:124
msgid ""
"By default, files are stored using an `SHA-1 hash`_ of their URLs for the "
"file names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:126
msgid "For example, the following image URL::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:128
msgid "http://www.example.com/image.jpg"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:130
msgid "Whose ``SHA-1 hash`` is::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:132
msgid "3afec3b4765f8f0a07b78f98c07b83f013567a0a"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:134
msgid ""
"Will be downloaded and stored using your chosen :ref:`storage method <topics-"
"supported-storage>` and the following file name::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:136
msgid "3afec3b4765f8f0a07b78f98c07b83f013567a0a.jpg"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:139
msgid "Custom File Naming"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:141
msgid ""
"You may wish to use a different calculated file name for saved files. For "
"example, classifying an image by including meta in the file name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:144
msgid ""
"Customize file names by overriding the ``file_path`` method of your media "
"pipeline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:147
msgid "For example, an image pipeline with image URL::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:149
msgid "http://www.example.com/product/images/large/front/0000000004166"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:151
msgid ""
"Can be processed into a file name with a condensed hash and the perspective "
"``front``::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:154
msgid "00b08510e4_front.jpg"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:156
msgid "By overriding ``file_path`` like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:158
msgid ""
"import hashlib\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def file_path(self, request, response=None, info=None, *, item=None):\n"
"    image_url_hash = hashlib.shake_256(request.url.encode()).hexdigest(5)\n"
"    image_perspective = request.url.split(\"/\")[-2]\n"
"    image_filename = f\"{image_url_hash}_{image_perspective}.jpg\"\n"
"\n"
"    return image_filename"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:171
msgid ""
"If your custom file name scheme relies on meta data that can vary between "
"scrapes it may lead to unexpected re-downloading of existing media using new "
"file names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:175
msgid ""
"For example, if your custom file name scheme uses a product title and the "
"site changes an item's product title between scrapes, Scrapy will re-"
"download the same media using updated file names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:179
msgid ""
"For more information about the ``file_path`` method, see :ref:`topics-media-"
"pipeline-override`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:184
msgid "Naming files after the response"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:186
msgid ""
"``file_path`` also receives the ``response``, which allows naming files "
"after response data. For example, to determine the file extension from the "
"``Content-Type`` header, for URLs that do not end in a file name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:190
msgid ""
"import mimetypes\n"
"\n"
"from scrapy.pipelines.files import FilesPipeline\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"class ContentTypeFilesPipeline(FilesPipeline):\n"
"    def file_path(self, request, response=None, info=None, *, item=None):\n"
"        path = super().file_path(request, response, info, item=item)\n"
"        if response is None:\n"
"            return path\n"
"        content_type = response.headers[\"Content-Type\"].decode()\n"
"        return path + (mimetypes.guess_extension(content_type) or \"\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:205
msgid ""
"This requires setting :setting:`FILES_EXPIRES` to ``0``. To find out whether "
"a file has already been downloaded, Scrapy calls ``file_path`` before the "
"download, with ``response`` set to ``None``, and checks the age of the file "
"at the resulting path. A path that depends on the response can never match "
"that check, and :setting:`FILES_EXPIRES` set to ``0`` disables it, at the "
"cost of downloading every file on every run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:215
msgid "Setting request headers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:217
msgid ""
"Media requests are built from the item, not from the response that yielded "
"it, so features like :class:`~scrapy.spidermiddlewares.referer."
"RefererMiddleware` do not apply to them. To send a header such as "
"``Referer``, store the value on the item in your spider, and read it back "
"from the item in ``get_media_requests`` of your custom media pipeline:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:223
msgid ""
"from scrapy import Request, Spider\n"
"from scrapy.pipelines.files import FilesPipeline\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"class MySpider(Spider):\n"
"    def parse(self, response):\n"
"        yield {\n"
"            \"file_urls\": response.css(\"a.file::attr(href)\").getall(),\n"
"            \"referrer\": response.url,\n"
"        }\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"class MyFilesPipeline(FilesPipeline):\n"
"    def get_media_requests(self, item, info):\n"
"        for file_url in item[\"file_urls\"]:\n"
"            yield Request(file_url, headers={\"Referer\": "
"item[\"referrer\"]})"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:245
msgid "Supported Storage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:247
msgid ""
"Use :setting:`UPLOAD_TIMEOUT` to limit how long uploads to a remote storage "
"backend may take."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:251
msgid "File system storage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:253
msgid "File system storage will save files to the following path::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:255
msgid "<IMAGES_STORE>/full/<FILE_NAME>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:257
#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:533
msgid "Where:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:259
msgid ""
"``<IMAGES_STORE>`` is the directory defined in :setting:`IMAGES_STORE` "
"setting for the Images Pipeline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:262
msgid ""
"``full`` is a sub-directory to separate full images from thumbnails (if "
"used). For more info see :ref:`topics-images-thumbnails`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:265
msgid ""
"``<FILE_NAME>`` is the file name assigned to the file.  For more info see :"
"ref:`topics-file-naming`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:271
msgid "FTP server storage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:273
msgid ""
":setting:`FILES_STORE` and :setting:`IMAGES_STORE` can point to an FTP "
"server. Scrapy will automatically upload the files to the server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:276
msgid ""
":setting:`FILES_STORE` and :setting:`IMAGES_STORE` should be written in one "
"of the following forms::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:279
msgid ""
"ftp://username:password@address:port/path\n"
"ftp://address:port/path"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:282
msgid ""
"If ``username`` and ``password`` are not provided, they are taken from the :"
"setting:`FTP_USER` and :setting:`FTP_PASSWORD` settings respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:285
msgid ""
"FTP supports two different connection modes: active or passive. Scrapy uses "
"the passive connection mode by default. To use the active connection mode "
"instead, set the :setting:`FEED_STORAGE_FTP_ACTIVE` setting to ``True``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:292
msgid "Amazon S3 storage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:294
msgid "Requires the :ref:`s3 <extras>` extra."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:299
msgid ""
":setting:`FILES_STORE` and :setting:`IMAGES_STORE` can represent an Amazon "
"S3 bucket. Scrapy will automatically upload the files to the bucket."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:302
msgid "For example, this is a valid :setting:`IMAGES_STORE` value:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:304
msgid "IMAGES_STORE = \"s3://bucket/images\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:308
msgid ""
"You can modify the Access Control List (ACL) policy used for the stored "
"files, which is defined by the :setting:`FILES_STORE_S3_ACL` and :setting:"
"`IMAGES_STORE_S3_ACL` settings. By default, the ACL is set to ``private``. "
"To make the files publicly available use the ``public-read`` policy:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:314
msgid "IMAGES_STORE_S3_ACL = \"public-read\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:318
msgid ""
"For more information, see `canned ACLs`_ in the Amazon S3 Developer Guide."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:320
msgid ""
"To send custom headers with the uploaded files, subclass ``S3FilesStore`` "
"with a different ``HEADERS`` class attribute, and point the ``s3`` scheme of "
"your pipeline to it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:324
msgid ""
"from scrapy.pipelines.files import FilesPipeline, S3FilesStore\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"class CustomS3FilesStore(S3FilesStore):\n"
"    HEADERS = {\n"
"        \"Cache-Control\": \"max-age=172800\",\n"
"        \"X-Amz-Storage-Class\": \"STANDARD_IA\",\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"class CustomFilesPipeline(FilesPipeline):\n"
"    STORE_SCHEMES = FilesPipeline.STORE_SCHEMES | {\"s3\": "
"CustomS3FilesStore}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:339
msgid ""
"Supported headers are those that the installed botocore version models for "
"the `PutObject`_ operation; any other header raises :exc:`TypeError`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:342
msgid ""
"You can also use other S3-like storages. Storages like self-hosted `Minio`_ "
"or `Zenko CloudServer`_. All you need to do is set the endpoint option in "
"your Scrapy settings:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:346
msgid "AWS_ENDPOINT_URL = \"http://minio.example.com:9000\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:350
msgid ""
"For self-hosting you also might feel the need not to use SSL and not to "
"verify SSL connection:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:352
msgid ""
"AWS_USE_SSL = False  # or True (None by default)\n"
"AWS_VERIFY = False  # or True (None by default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:357
msgid ""
"To reuse connections for as many files as you check or upload in parallel, "
"set :setting:`AWS_MAX_POOL_CONNECTIONS` accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:369
msgid "Google Cloud Storage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:371
msgid "Requires the :ref:`gcs <extras>` extra."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:376
msgid ""
":setting:`FILES_STORE` and :setting:`IMAGES_STORE` can represent a Google "
"Cloud Storage bucket. Scrapy will automatically upload the files to the "
"bucket."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:379
msgid ""
"For example, these are valid :setting:`IMAGES_STORE` and :setting:"
"`GCS_PROJECT_ID` settings:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:381
msgid ""
"IMAGES_STORE = \"gs://bucket/images/\"\n"
"GCS_PROJECT_ID = \"project_id\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:386
msgid "For information about authentication, see this `documentation`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:390
msgid ""
"You can modify the Access Control List (ACL) policy used for the stored "
"files, which is defined by the :setting:`FILES_STORE_GCS_ACL` and :setting:"
"`IMAGES_STORE_GCS_ACL` settings. By default, the ACL is set to ``''`` (empty "
"string) which means that Cloud Storage applies the bucket's default object "
"ACL to the object. To make the files publicly available use the "
"``publicRead`` policy:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:397
msgid "IMAGES_STORE_GCS_ACL = \"publicRead\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:401
msgid ""
"For more information, see `Predefined ACLs`_ in the Google Cloud Platform "
"Developer Guide."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:406
msgid "Usage example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:413
msgid ""
"In order to use a media pipeline, first :ref:`enable it <topics-media-"
"pipeline-enabling>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:416
msgid ""
"Then, if a spider returns an :ref:`item object <topics-items>` with the URLs "
"field (``file_urls`` or ``image_urls``, for the Files or Images Pipeline "
"respectively), the pipeline will put the results under the respective field "
"(``files`` or ``images``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:421
msgid ""
"When using :ref:`item types <item-types>` for which fields are defined "
"beforehand, you must define both the URLs field and the results field. For "
"example, when using the images pipeline, items must define both the "
"``image_urls`` and the ``images`` field. For instance, using a dataclass:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:426
msgid ""
"from dataclasses import dataclass, field\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"@dataclass\n"
"class MyItem:\n"
"    # ... other item fields ...\n"
"    image_urls: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n"
"    images: list[dict] = field(default_factory=list)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:437
msgid ""
"If you want to use another field name for the URLs key or for the results "
"key, it is also possible to override it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:440
msgid ""
"For the Files Pipeline, set :setting:`FILES_URLS_FIELD` and/or :setting:"
"`FILES_RESULT_FIELD` settings:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:443
msgid ""
"FILES_URLS_FIELD = \"field_name_for_your_files_urls\"\n"
"FILES_RESULT_FIELD = \"field_name_for_your_processed_files\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:448
msgid ""
"For the Images Pipeline, set :setting:`IMAGES_URLS_FIELD` and/or :setting:"
"`IMAGES_RESULT_FIELD` settings:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:451
msgid ""
"IMAGES_URLS_FIELD = \"field_name_for_your_images_urls\"\n"
"IMAGES_RESULT_FIELD = \"field_name_for_your_processed_images\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:456
msgid ""
"If you need something more complex and want to override the custom pipeline "
"behaviour, see :ref:`topics-media-pipeline-override`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:459
msgid ""
"If you have multiple image pipelines inheriting from :class:`ImagesPipeline` "
"and you want to have different settings in different pipelines you can set "
"setting keys preceded with uppercase name of your pipeline class. E.g. if "
"your pipeline is called ``MyPipeline`` and you want to have custom :setting:"
"`IMAGES_URLS_FIELD` you define setting ``MYPIPELINE_IMAGES_URLS_FIELD`` and "
"your custom settings will be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:468
msgid "Additional features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:473
msgid "File expiration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:478
msgid ""
"The Image Pipeline avoids downloading files that were downloaded recently. "
"To adjust this retention delay use the :setting:`FILES_EXPIRES` setting (or :"
"setting:`IMAGES_EXPIRES`, in case of Images Pipeline), which specifies the "
"delay in number of days:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:483
msgid ""
"# 120 days of delay for files expiration\n"
"FILES_EXPIRES = 120\n"
"\n"
"# 30 days of delay for images expiration\n"
"IMAGES_EXPIRES = 30"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:491
msgid ""
"The default value for both settings is 90 days. A negative value disables "
"expiration, i.e. files are never re-downloaded once fetched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:494
msgid ""
"If you have a pipeline that subclasses FilesPipeline and you'd like to have "
"a different setting for it, you can set setting keys preceded by the "
"uppercase class name. For example, given a pipeline class called MyPipeline "
"you can set the setting key:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:499
msgid "MYPIPELINE_FILES_EXPIRES = 180"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:501
msgid ""
"and the pipeline class MyPipeline will have an expiration time set to 180."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:503
msgid ""
"The last modified time from the file is used to determine the age of the "
"file in days, which is then compared to the set expiration time to determine "
"if the file is expired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:509
msgid "Thumbnail generation for images"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:511
msgid ""
"The Images Pipeline can automatically create thumbnails of the downloaded "
"images."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:516
msgid ""
"In order to use this feature, you must set :setting:`IMAGES_THUMBS` to a "
"dictionary where the keys are the thumbnail names and the values are their "
"dimensions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:519
#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:581
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:521
msgid ""
"IMAGES_THUMBS = {\n"
"    \"small\": (50, 50),\n"
"    \"big\": (270, 270),\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:528
msgid ""
"When you use this feature, the Images Pipeline will create thumbnails of the "
"each specified size with this format::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:531
msgid "<IMAGES_STORE>/thumbs/<size_name>/<image_id>.jpg"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:535
msgid ""
"``<size_name>`` is the one specified in the :setting:`IMAGES_THUMBS` "
"dictionary keys (``small``, ``big``, etc)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:538
msgid "``<image_id>`` is the `SHA-1 hash`_ of the image url"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:542
msgid ""
"Example of image files stored using ``small`` and ``big`` thumbnail names::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:544
msgid ""
"<IMAGES_STORE>/full/63bbfea82b8880ed33cdb762aa11fab722a90a24.jpg\n"
"<IMAGES_STORE>/thumbs/small/63bbfea82b8880ed33cdb762aa11fab722a90a24.jpg\n"
"<IMAGES_STORE>/thumbs/big/63bbfea82b8880ed33cdb762aa11fab722a90a24.jpg"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:548
msgid "The first one is the full image, as downloaded from the site."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:553
msgid "Preserving the original image format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:557
msgid ""
"By default, the Images Pipeline converts every image to JPEG, flattening "
"transparency onto a white background. Set :setting:`IMAGES_PRESERVE_FORMAT` "
"to ``True`` to keep each image, and its thumbnails, in the format it was "
"downloaded in instead:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:562
msgid "IMAGES_PRESERVE_FORMAT = True"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:566
msgid ""
"Stored files then get no extension, since the actual format is only known "
"once the image has been downloaded; see :ref:`file-naming-response` to "
"derive one from the response instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:571
msgid "Filtering out small images"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:577
msgid ""
"When using the Images Pipeline, you can drop images which are too small, by "
"specifying the minimum allowed size in the :setting:`IMAGES_MIN_HEIGHT` and :"
"setting:`IMAGES_MIN_WIDTH` settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:583
msgid ""
"IMAGES_MIN_HEIGHT = 110\n"
"IMAGES_MIN_WIDTH = 110"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:589
msgid "The size constraints don't affect thumbnail generation at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:591
msgid ""
"It is possible to set just one size constraint or both. When setting both of "
"them, only images that satisfy both minimum sizes will be saved. For the "
"above example, images of sizes (105 x 105) or (105 x 200) or (200 x 105) "
"will all be dropped because at least one dimension is shorter than the "
"constraint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:596
msgid "By default, there are no size constraints, so all images are processed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:599
msgid "Allowing redirections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:603
msgid ""
"By default media pipelines ignore redirects, i.e. an HTTP redirection to a "
"media file URL request will mean the media download is considered failed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:606
msgid "To handle media redirections, set this setting to ``True``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:608
msgid "MEDIA_ALLOW_REDIRECTS = True"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:613
msgid "Limiting the result cache"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:617
msgid ""
"Media pipelines remember the outcome of every media request they handle, so "
"that a file referenced by several items is downloaded once. By default every "
"outcome is kept for the whole crawl, which takes about 600 bytes per "
"distinct media URL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:624
msgid ""
"To cap that memory, set :setting:`MEDIA_CACHE_SIZE` to the number of most "
"recently used outcomes to keep, or to ``0`` to keep none:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:627
msgid "MEDIA_CACHE_SIZE = 10000"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:634
msgid "Extending the Media Pipelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:638
msgid ""
"See here the methods that you can override in your custom Files Pipeline:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:644
#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:795
msgid ""
"This method is called once per downloaded item. It returns the download path "
"of the file originating from the specified :class:`response <scrapy.http."
"Response>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:648
#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:799
msgid ""
"In addition to ``response``, this method receives the original :class:"
"`request <scrapy.Request>`, :class:`info <scrapy.pipelines.media."
"MediaPipeline.SpiderInfo>` and :class:`item <scrapy.Item>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:653
#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:804
msgid ""
"You can override this method to customize the download path of each file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:655
#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:806
msgid ""
"For example, if file URLs end like regular paths (e.g. ``https://example.com/"
"a/b/c/foo.png``), you can use the following approach to download all files "
"into the ``files`` folder with their original filenames (e.g. ``files/foo."
"png``):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:660
msgid ""
"from pathlib import PurePosixPath\n"
"from scrapy.utils.httpobj import urlparse_cached\n"
"\n"
"from scrapy.pipelines.files import FilesPipeline\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"class MyFilesPipeline(FilesPipeline):\n"
"    def file_path(self, request, response=None, info=None, *, item=None):\n"
"        return \"files/\" + PurePosixPath(urlparse_cached(request).path).name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:672
#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:823
msgid ""
"Similarly, you can use the ``item`` to determine the file path based on some "
"item property, or the ``response``, see :ref:`file-naming-response`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:675
#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:826
msgid ""
"By default the :meth:`file_path` method returns ``full/<request URL hash>."
"<extension>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:680
msgid ""
"As seen on the workflow, the pipeline will get the requests for the files to "
"download from the item by calling this method. You can override it to change "
"what requests are returned:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:684
msgid ""
"from itemadapter import ItemAdapter\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def get_media_requests(self, item, info):\n"
"    adapter = ItemAdapter(item)\n"
"    for file_url in adapter[\"file_urls\"]:\n"
"        yield scrapy.Request(file_url)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:694
msgid ""
"You can also use it to set request headers, see :ref:`media-request-headers`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:696
msgid ""
"Those requests will be processed by the pipeline and, when they have "
"finished downloading, the results will be sent to the :meth:"
"`~item_completed` method, as a list of 2-element tuples. Each tuple will "
"contain ``(success, file_info_or_error)`` where:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:701
msgid ""
"``success`` is a boolean which is ``True`` if the image was downloaded "
"successfully or ``False`` if it failed for some reason"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:704
msgid ""
"``file_info_or_error`` is a dict containing the following keys (if success "
"is ``True``) or a :exc:`~twisted.python.failure.Failure` if there was a "
"problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:708
msgid ""
"``url`` - the url where the file was downloaded from. This is the url of the "
"request returned from the :meth:`~get_media_requests` method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:712
msgid ""
"``path`` - the path (relative to :setting:`FILES_STORE`) where the file was "
"stored"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:715
msgid "``checksum`` - a `MD5 hash`_ of the image contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:717
msgid "``status`` - the file status indication."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:719
msgid "It can be one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:721
msgid "``downloaded`` - file was downloaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:722
msgid ""
"``uptodate`` - file was not downloaded, as it was downloaded recently, "
"according to the file expiration policy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:724
msgid ""
"``cached`` - file was taken from a cache (the response has a ``\"cached\"`` "
"flag, e.g. from :class:`~scrapy.downloadermiddlewares.httpcache."
"HttpCacheMiddleware`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:728
msgid ""
"The list of tuples received by :meth:`~item_completed` is guaranteed to "
"retain the same order of the requests returned from the :meth:"
"`~get_media_requests` method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:732
msgid "Here's a typical value of the ``results`` argument:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:738
msgid ""
"[\n"
"    (\n"
"        True,\n"
"        {\n"
"            \"checksum\": \"2b00042f7481c7b056c4b410d28f33cf\",\n"
"            \"path\": \"full/0a79c461a4062ac383dc4fade7bc09f1384a3910."
"jpg\",\n"
"            \"url\": \"http://www.example.com/files/product1.pdf\",\n"
"            \"status\": \"downloaded\",\n"
"        },\n"
"    ),\n"
"    (False, Failure(...)),\n"
"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:755
msgid ""
"The :meth:`FilesPipeline.item_completed` method called when all file "
"requests for a single item have completed (either finished downloading, or "
"failed for some reason)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:759
msgid ""
"The :meth:`~item_completed` method must return the output that will be sent "
"to subsequent item pipeline stages, so you must return (or drop) the item, "
"as you would in any pipeline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:763
msgid ""
"Here is an example of the :meth:`~item_completed` method where we store the "
"downloaded file paths (passed in results) in the ``file_paths`` item field, "
"and we drop the item if it doesn't contain any files:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:767
msgid ""
"from itemadapter import ItemAdapter\n"
"from scrapy.exceptions import DropItem\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def item_completed(self, results, item, info):\n"
"    file_paths = [x[\"path\"] for ok, x in results if ok]\n"
"    if not file_paths:\n"
"        raise DropItem(\"Item contains no files\")\n"
"    adapter = ItemAdapter(item)\n"
"    adapter[\"file_paths\"] = file_paths\n"
"    return item"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:781
#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:865
msgid "By default, the :meth:`item_completed` method returns the item."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:786
msgid ""
"See here the methods that you can override in your custom Images Pipeline:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/media-pipeline.rst:790
msgid ""
"The :class:`ImagesPipeline` is an extension of the :class:`FilesPipeline`, "
"customizing the field names and adding custom behavior for images."
